Decide, in this order:
1. Is the cited sink real (file + Class.method or file:line exists)?
2. Is the code dead / not shipped / unreachable from a running local app?
3. What sits in front of the sink (auth filter, role check, CSRF, allowlist, parameterization, encoding, feature flag, network-only-admin)?
4. Who must the attacker already be: unauthenticated, authenticated user, or admin?
5. How hard to exploit locally (low / medium / high) given those preconditions?
6. Verdict: exploitable | not_exploitable | false_positive | dead_code | needs_runtime

